Ah, but, brown puddings multiply if you chop them, and there are no gremlins (in
quantity) before the first Castle.  This makes things a tiny bit different.

  I have played (in a very superficial way) Moria, where there are gnats which
multiply.  It si impossible to kill them after a while.  Since rooms in Hack
are less well "closed" than those in Moria, the game would fill up with the
things, and you wouldn't be able to move without a freshly painted wall to watch
drying.

